  "content": {
    "id": "p62-q7",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "IQ scores are normally distributed with mean 100. 10% of the population score above 125. Find the standard deviation to 1 d.p.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sigma=19.5$",
      "worked": "$P(X\\le125)=1-0.10=0.90$.\n\nUsing inverse normal, $z=\\operatorname{invNorm}(0.90)\\approx1.2815516$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}z&=\\frac{125-100}{\\sigma}\\\\125&=100+z\\sigma\\\\\\sigma&=\\frac{25}{z}\\\\&\\approx19.5\\quad\\text{(1 d.p.)}\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
